# FleetLink React Native Standards

## Components

- **Functional components only** — no class components, ever
- **One component per file** — file name matches component name
- **Presentational by default** — screens compose; components receive props and emit events
- **Small components** — if JSX exceeds ~60 lines, extract sub-components

```tsx
// TripCard.tsx — presentational
interface TripCardProps {
  trip: Trip;
  onPress: (tripId: string) => void;
}

export function TripCard({ trip, onPress }: TripCardProps) {
  return (
    <Pressable onPress={() => onPress(trip.id)} style={styles.card}>
      <Text style={styles.route}>{trip.pickup} → {trip.dropoff}</Text>
      <Text style={styles.fare}>{formatCurrency(trip.fare)}</Text>
    </Pressable>
  );
}
```

## Styles — Separate Files, No Inline

```tsx
// TripCard.styles.ts
import { StyleSheet } from 'react-native';
import { spacing, colors, typography } from '@/shared/theme';

export const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  card: {
    padding: spacing.md,
    backgroundColor: colors.surface,
    borderRadius: spacing.sm,
    marginBottom: spacing.sm,
  },
  route: {
    ...typography.body,
    color: colors.textPrimary,
  },
});
```

**Rules:**
- Every component with styles has a `.styles.ts` sibling file
- No inline `style={{ }}` — except truly dynamic values (e.g., `{ width: progress * 100 }`)
- Even dynamic values should use theme tokens: `colors.primary`, not `'#2563eb'`

## Theme — Light & Dark Mode

```tsx
// Use theme hook — never hardcode colors
const { colors } = useTheme();

<Text style={[styles.title, { color: colors.textPrimary }]} />
```

- All colors from `shared/theme/colors.ts` — light and dark palettes
- `useTheme()` hook reads Zustand/MMKV preference + system setting
- Test every new screen in both light and dark mode
- StatusBar style adapts to theme

## Theme Tokens (Required)

```typescript
// shared/theme/
colors.ts      // light + dark palettes
spacing.ts     // 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48
typography.ts  // heading, body, caption, label
radius.ts      // sm, md, lg, full
shadows.ts     // card, modal
```

Never use raw numbers for spacing in components — use `spacing.md`, etc.

## Navigation

- React Navigation with typed routes (`RootStackParamList`)
- Route params: pass IDs, not full objects
- Screen files live in `features/{name}/screens/`
- Navigation logic in hooks or screen — not in shared components
- Deep linking configured per feature as needed

```typescript
// app/navigation/types.ts
export type RootStackParamList = {
  TripDetail: { tripId: string };
  DriverProfile: { driverId: string };
};
```

## Screens Pattern

```tsx
// features/trips/screens/TripListScreen.tsx
export function TripListScreen() {
  const { data, isLoading, isError, refetch } = useTrips();
  const navigation = useNavigation<TripListNav>();

  if (isLoading) return <TripListSkeleton />;
  if (isError) return <ErrorState onRetry={refetch} />;
  if (!data?.length) return <EmptyState title="No trips" />;

  return <TripList trips={data} onTripPress={(id) => navigation.navigate('TripDetail', { tripId: id })} />;
}
```

Screen = thin orchestrator. No Axios. No business logic.

## Hooks

- Feature hooks in `features/{name}/hooks/`
- Shared hooks in `shared/hooks/`
- Query hooks wrap React Query + service
- One hook per concern (`useTrips`, `useAcceptTrip` — not `useTripEverything`)

## Responsive Layouts

- Use `flex` — avoid fixed pixel widths for containers
- Use `useWindowDimensions` or percentage for adaptive layouts
- Safe area via `SafeAreaView` or `useSafeAreaInsets`
- Test on small (iPhone SE) and large (Pro Max) simulators
- Tablet: consider two-column layouts where appropriate

## Accessibility

- `accessibilityLabel` on interactive elements without visible text
- Minimum touch target 44x44
- Sufficient color contrast in both themes

## Anti-Patterns

| Pattern | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| Class component | Functional + hooks |
| `StyleSheet` inline in component file | Separate `.styles.ts` |
| Hardcoded `#fff`, `#000` | Theme tokens |
| 300-line screen component | Split into sub-components + hook |
| `navigation.navigate` in shared Button | Pass `onPress` from screen |
| `fetch()` in component | Service + React Query hook |
